},{"s":12.12,"e":15.54,"text":"What if the greatest victory"},{"s":15.54,"e":20.48,"text":"sent every soldier back?"},{"s":20.48,"e":20.98,"text":"**[Verse 1 – rap]**"},{"s":22.26,"e":25.44,"text":"They said pick a side, I said pick up the pieces,"},{"s":25.36,"e":27.96,"text":"Peace got a price, but revenge never ceases."},{"s":27.96,"e":30.66,"text":"Preachers preach peace while the presidents posture,"},{"s":30.86,"e":33.26,"text":"Families fracture while the cameras capture."},{"s":33.32,"e":35.66,"text":"Maps get marked by a man in a room,"},{"s":35.66,"e":38.34,"text":"Then a mother gets flowers where a son used to bloom."},{"s":38.54,"e":41.08,"text":"Medals on a mantle, names carved in granite,"},{"s":41.54,"e":43.48,"text":"Everybody screaming they’re defending the planet."},{"s":43.48,"e":45.98,"text":"But tell me who won when the playground burned?"},{"s":46.2,"e":48.66,"text":"Who gained ground when the children never returned?"},{"s":48.78,"e":50.84,"text":"Who conquered what when the hospitals fell?"},{"s":51.1,"e":55.72,"text":"If victory looks like this, victory looks like hell."},{"s":55.72,"e":56.22,"text":"**[Pre-Chorus – female vocal]**"},{"s":55.72,"e":57.76,"text":"Bring them home, bring them home,"},{"s":58.36,"e":60.76,"text":"Let the babies grow old."},{"s":61.36,"e":62.68,"text":"Let the stories get written"},{"s":63.44,"e":65.54,"text":"without names carved in stone."},{"s":65.54,"e":66.04,"text":"**[Chorus – massive duet]**"},{"s":65.76,"e":68.72,"text":"**I want a win where nobody dies,**"},{"s":68.72,"e":73.52,"text":"No smoke in the sun, no fire in the skies."},{"s":73.44,"e":76.26,"text":"No mother on the phone asking heaven why,"},{"s":76.26,"e":79.22,"text":"No folded-up flag where her child should lie."},{"s":79.22,"e":81.62,"text":"**Give me a victory with nobody dead,**"},{"s":81.62,"e":84.34,"text":"Bread on the table, not bloodshed instead."},{"s":84.34,"e":87.06,"text":"Hands held high but no guns overhead—"},{"s":88.26,"e":91.76,"text":"**That’s my kind of victory: nobody dead.**"},{"s":91.76,"e":92.26,"text":"**[Verse 2 – rap]**"},{"s":91.76,"e":94.2,"text":"Real strength ain’t rage, real power is patience,"},{"s":94.2,"e":96.62,"text":"Talk through the tension, transform the nations."},{"s":96.62,"e":98.98,"text":"Courage is calling when hatred says hide,"},{"s":98.98,"e":101.86,"text":"Finding some humanity over the divide."},{"s":101.86,"e":103.22,"text":"The enemy eats, the enemy sleeps,"},{"s":103.22,"e":104.52,"text":"The enemy laughs and the enemy weeps."},{"s":104.52,"e":107,"text":"The enemy’s daughter draws stars on a page,"},{"s":106.92,"e":110.16,"text":"The enemy’s father gets scared and gets aged."},{"s":111.02,"e":113.96,"text":"Same little heartbeat, same oxygen breath,"},{"s":113.96,"e":116.58,"text":"Same desperate instinct to bargain with death."},{"s":116.58,"e":119.24,"text":"Different translation, identical prayer:"},{"s":119.24,"e":121.84,"text":"“Please bring my family home from out there.”"},{"s":121.84,"e":124.42,"text":"So cancel the countdown, cut through the pride,"},{"s":124.42,"e":127.02,"text":"Put diplomats deep where the missiles would ride."},{"s":127.02,"e":129.74,"text":"If somebody tells me compassion is weak,"},{"s":129.74,"e":132.68,"text":"I’ll tell ’em restraint takes the strength of the meek."},{"s":132.68,"e":133.18,"text":"**[Pre-Chorus]**"},{"s":133.8,"e":136.28,"text":"Bring them home, bring them home,"},{"s":136.28,"e":138.56,"text":"Every daughter, every son."},{"s":138.56,"e":140.82,"text":"The greatest war we’ll ever win"},{"s":140.82,"e":143.56,"text":"is the war that never comes."},{"s":143.56,"e":144.06,"text":"**[Chorus]**"},{"s":144.24,"e":146.94,"text":"**I want a win where nobody dies,**"},{"s":146.94,"e":151.74,"text":"No smoke in the sun, no fire in the skies."},{"s":151.66,"e":154.52,"text":"No mother on the phone asking heaven why,"},{"s":154.52,"e":157.48,"text":"No folded-up flag where her child should lie."},{"s":157.48,"e":159.94,"text":"**Give me a victory with nobody dead,**"},{"s":159.94,"e":162.58,"text":"Bread on the table, not bloodshed instead."},{"s":162.58,"e":165.2,"text":"Hands held high but no guns overhead—"},{"s":166.56,"e":170.18,"text":"**That’s my kind of victory: nobody dead.**"},{"s":170.18,"e":170.68,"text":"**[Bridge – stripped piano / female lead]**"},{"s":170.18,"e":172.5,"text":"What if mercy made the headlines?"},{"s":172.86,"e":175.24,"text":"What if treaties topped the charts?"},{"s":175.48,"e":177.66,"text":"What if leaders measured greatness"},{"s":177.66,"e":179.98,"text":"by the number of beating hearts?"},{"s":180.2,"e":182.26,"text":"No revenge passed down like inheritance,"},{"s":182.26,"e":184.8,"text":"No child taught an ancient arrogance."},{"s":184.8,"e":187.2,"text":"Let tomorrow wake without yesterday’s debt—"},{"s":187.16,"e":188.85,"text":"Forgive what we can."},{"s":189.46,"e":190.44,"text":"Prevent what comes next."},{"s":190.44,"e":190.94,"text":"**[Final Rap – drums build]**"},{"s":190.44,"e":193.02,"text":"Let the tanks turn tractors, let the trenches grow trees,"},{"s":193.02,"e":195.62,"text":"Let the factories manufacture medicine and peace."},{"s":195.62,"e":198.1,"text":"Let the pilots fly people safely back home,"},{"s":198.1,"e":200.78,"text":"Let the drones shoot movies, let the battlefields grow."},{"s":200.78,"e":203,"text":"Spend the billions on bridges, on bedrooms, on bread,"},{"s":203,"e":205.4,"text":"On keeping people living instead of counting the dead."},{"s":205.4,"e":208.02,"text":"Call me naïve—I’d rather be that"},{"s":208.02,"e":210.6,"text":"Than clever enough to make a cemetery map."},{"s":210.8,"e":213.24,"text":"We’ve mastered destruction, now master restraint,"},{"s":213.24,"e":215.82,"text":"Make peace look powerful, make mercy look great."},{"s":215.82,"e":218.5,"text":"The hardest flex left on this planet instead"},{"s":218.5,"e":219.94,"text":"Is winning the whole thing—"},{"s":219.94,"e":222.18,"text":"**with nobody dead.**"},{"s":222.18,"e":222.68,"text":"**[Final Chorus – huge choir + rap ad-libs]**"},{"s":222.56,"e":225.22,"text":"**I want a win where nobody dies,**"},{"s":225.22,"e":229.82,"text":"No smoke in the sun, no fire in the skies."},{"s":229.82,"e":232.44,"text":"Every mother gets her child back alive,"},{"s":232.44,"e":237.64,"text":"Every enemy becomes somebody we survived **with**."},{"s":237.78,"e":240.62,"text":"**Give me a victory with nobody dead,**"},{"s":240.62,"e":243.08,"text":"Hope in the heart and a roof overhead."},{"s":243.08,"e":248.12,"text":"Stars still shining when the history gets read—"},{"s":248.12,"e":255.98,"text":"**That’s my kind of victory: nobody dead.**"},{"s":255.98,"e":257.58,"text":"Nobody dead."},{"s":257.58,"e":258.58,"text":"Everybody fed."},{"s":258.58,"e":260.06,"text":"Nobody dead."},{"s":260.06,"e":263.06,"text":"Let tomorrow live instead."},{"s":271.66,"e":274.24,"text":"**Nobody dead.**"}],"duration":279.4,"source":"whisper-aligned","generatedAt":"2026-08-29T02:49:44.613Z","stats":{"whisperWords":651,"polishedWords":629,"matched":588,"matchRate":0.935}}